From 6bc5fb073af183638de9cd93e43ab6430eaf1b82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 18:53:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05362/11362] [outer-loop] build a verifier and test it against
 a cheap baseline on the MMLU-Pro headroom corpus: honest negative,
 underpowered at n=40

Direct follow-up to the operator request: 'build a verifier and test whether
it actually beats a cheap baseline on this corpus.'

Regenerated the same 40-question MMLU-Pro corpus with FULL candidate
reasoning text saved (the prior headroom-check script only persisted parsed
letters, not enough for a verifier to train on). Built a learned verifier
(all-MiniLM-L6-v2 + LogisticRegression) and a matched cheap baseline (8
non-learned text-statistical features + LogisticRegression), both via
leave-one-question-out CV, both used to select the top-scored candidate
among K=6 per question.

Result: oracle_at_k_ceiling=0.300, sc_vote_accuracy=0.075,
verifier_selection_accuracy=0.100, cheap_baseline_selection_accuracy=0.075.
Verifier delta vs cheap baseline: +0.025, CI95=[-0.100, 0.150] -- includes 0,
not significant. The verifier does NOT beat the cheap baseline. Honest
reason: n_questions=40 with only 20/240 correct candidate rows is a
genuinely underpowered test for a per-candidate classifier via 40-fold CV,
not strong evidence against the underlying hypothesis. adversarial_verify:
0 flagged (fixed 5 TAUTOLOGY flags along the way -- 3 were genuinely
redundant duplicate field names, 2 were real small-n coincidences now
disclosed in prose per the established pattern).

Infrastructure: generation was interrupted 5 times by what appears to be a
background-task lifecycle limit in this environment (server processes died
independent of script correctness). Fixed via resumable checkpointing
(flush-per-candidate, requiring FULL K_SAMPLES coverage before marking a
question done -- caught and fixed a real bug where a partially-generated
question would otherwise be silently under-sampled).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
